{
  "slug": "zeabur",
  "name": "Zeabur",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "CLI skills for deploying, managing, and troubleshooting services on Zeabur — a cloud deployment platform. Covers the full lifecycle: project creation, service deployment, template management, domain registration & DNS, server provisioning, environment variables, logs, and common issue diagnosis.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **32 skills**.\n\n- **Skills** (32): `zeabur-ai-hub` (Use when managing AI Hub account, API keys, balance, usage, or API endpoints), `zeabur-auth` (Use when logging in, logging out, or checking Zeabur auth status), `zeabur-cluster-scale` (Use when scaling a dedicated Kubernetes cluster (Linode LKE or AWS EKS) on Zeabur — listing node pools,…), `zeabur-database` (Use when deploying a database to Zeabur), `zeabur-deploy` (Use when deploying a local project or codebase to Zeabur), `zeabur-deployment-logs` (Use when viewing service runtime or build logs), `zeabur-dockerfile` (Use when generating a Dockerfile for deploying a project to Zeabur), `zeabur-domain-dns` (Use when managing DNS records for Zeabur-registered domains), and 24 more\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install zeabur@claude-community` from `zeabur/zeabur-claude-plugin`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude",
    "copilot",
    "antigravity",
    "codex"
  ],
